invariant: INV-5
file: pem_files.c
catches: pem_files_test
reason: the call takes a chain block and does not read its outer fields,
  so a block of other DER, or a certificate with a byte after it, joins
  the chain. Every client then refuses the server, and the operator sees
  no CH_EINVAL at provisioning. test_chain_framing writes both and
  requires CH_EINVAL.

--- old
        if (next != PEM_BLOCKS_READ || count == chain_max || count == UINT8_MAX ||
            !is_certificate(cert, cert_len)) {
--- new
        (void)is_certificate;
        if (next != PEM_BLOCKS_READ || count == chain_max || count == UINT8_MAX) {
